# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The Dockerfiles install dependencies from package-lock.json inside the image and then copy
# source over the top. Without this file `COPY apps/client/ apps/client/` also carries the
# host's `apps/client/node_modules` in — a Windows or macOS tree, complete with that platform's
# native bindings, landing on top of the linux ones npm just installed and shadowing them.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. 42 MB of Gradle intermediates and a compiled APK, none of which the image uses.
dist
**/dist
apps/client/android/app/build
apps/client/android/.gradle
apps/client/ios/App/build
*.apk

# Secrets and data. `.env` is read by compose at run time, never baked into a layer, and a
# keystore in an image is a keystore anyone who pulls it can sign with.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/keystore.properties
*.keystore
*.jks
data
backups

# The exercise library is fetched into ./media on first boot and mounted at run time — 140 MB
# that would otherwise be sent to the daemon on every build.
media
.devmedia

# Nothing here changes what gets built, and all of it invalidates layer caches.
.git
.github
.claude
docs
logo
# …except the vectors themselves. The web image copies the mark into the site's document root,
# so the nav and the hero draw the brand from the same file the store assets are cut from
# rather than from a PNG that has to be re-exported every time the mark moves.
!logo/*.svg
# `assets` here is the repository's own top-level folder, not `apps/site/assets` — a
# .dockerignore pattern without a slash matches at the root only. The two paths below are the
# exception: the web image copies the screenshots and the banner into the project site, so
# they are the one part of this folder a build genuinely needs. Anything matching `**/assets`
# added later would break that, silently, as a site with no pictures on it.
assets
!assets/screenshots
!assets/banner.png
**/*.md
!apps/*/README.md
# ...except this one, which would otherwise be copied into the document root by the web image
# and served at /README.md. Last matching pattern wins, so this line has to come after the
# negation above.
apps/site/README.md
